   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The function f is defined by \\( f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2 - 4}{x - 2} \\) for x < 2, \\( f(2) = 6 \\), and \\( f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2 + 4x - 12}{x^2 - 2x} \\) for x > 2. What is \\( \\lim_{x \\to 2} f(x) \\)?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Both branches give zero over zero at x = 2: 4 - 4 = 0 over 2 - 2 = 0 on the left, and 4 + 8 - 12 = 0 over 4 - 4 = 0 on the right. The value f(2) = 6 plays no part in the limit.",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "On the left, x^2 - 4 = (x - 2)(x + 2), so for x < 2 the branch equals x + 2, which approaches 4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "On the right, x^2 + 4x - 12 = (x - 2)(x + 6) and x^2 - 2x = x(x - 2), so for x > 2 the branch equals (x + 6)/x, which approaches 8/2 = 4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               6
            ],
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The one-sided limits agree, so the limit as x approaches 2 is 4.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
